Dear Mr. Akram,

3220
03:00:17,888 --> 03:00:22,275
I hope this email finds you well and not buried under a pile of unread messages,

3221
03:00:22,355 --> 03:00:27,920
existential dread, or both as is common with emails from 25 year olds with life questions.

3222
03:00:28,000 --> 03:00:30,920
Okay, email came six days ago. I saw it.

3223
03:00:31,000 --> 03:00:34,920
I'm a 25 year old Pakistani girl currently living and studying in Europe.

3224
03:00:35,000 --> 03:00:41,850
I am in my last semester of my master's program, which is a miracle in itself considering how much pasta pans.

3225
03:00:41,930 --> 03:00:44,215
panic and public transport delays I've survived.

3226
03:00:44,295 --> 03:00:48,841
I plan to settle here after graduating, which sounds more rebellious than it actually is,

3227
03:00:48,921 --> 03:00:53,190
but trust me, this decision alone has already caused a few raised eyebrows back home.

3228
03:00:53,270 --> 03:00:57,193
There's not much waiting for me in Pakistan career wise, aside from my family,

3229
03:00:57,273 --> 03:00:58,080
who I love dearly.

3230
03:00:58,160 --> 03:01:03,658
But what complicates everything is something I haven't had the courage to fully share with them yet.

3231
03:01:03,738 --> 03:01:05,955
Now to the core of the story, grab some chai.

3232
03:01:06,035 --> 03:01:07,954
This might need a sip or two.

3233
03:01:08,034 --> 03:01:09,020
There you go, ma'am.

3234
03:01:09,840 --> 03:01:12,413
During a winter school organized by our program,

3235
03:01:12,493 --> 03:01:16,968
bless those academic events that actually change lives, I met a guy, he's Italian,

3236
03:01:17,048 --> 03:01:24,549
in the same master's program and despite us never studying in the same university or even country thanks to the multi-track system,

3237
03:01:24,629 --> 03:01:26,800
we met, clicked and well, never unclicked.

3238
03:01:26,880 --> 03:01:32,855
That one week together was enough for us to confess our feelings before returning to our respective cities.

3239
03:01:32,935 --> 03:01:36,660
And almost two years later, we're still together, happier than ever.

3240
03:01:37,080 --> 03:01:43,800
We've been visiting each other every month. We travel together and honestly he's everything I ever hoped for in a partner.

3241
03:01:43,880 --> 03:01:47,000
Kind, honest, funny and grounded with strong morals.

3242
03:01:47,080 --> 03:01:52,400
And yes, we both see marriage in the near future, not because of pressure, but because we actually want to.

3243
03:01:52,480 --> 03:01:54,200
Now here comes the complicated part.

3244
03:01:54,280 --> 03:01:56,100
Cue dramatic music.

3245
03:01:56,180 --> 03:02:03,080
My family doesn't know. They're practicing Muslims and while they're open-minded about many things, I'm not sure how they will react to me.

3246
03:02:03,370 --> 03:02:05,416
Marrying someone who isn't a Muslim.

3247
03:02:05,496 --> 03:02:07,121
I've only confided in my aunt.

3248
03:02:07,201 --> 03:02:11,340
She's supportive but not optimistic about how my father might respond.

3249
03:02:11,920 --> 03:02:14,447
I've been clear with my boyfriend from the beginning.

3250
03:02:14,527 --> 03:02:18,024
In Islam, Muslim women aren't permitted to marry outside the religion.

3251
03:02:18,104 --> 03:02:19,535
He's never taken this lightly.

3252
03:02:19,615 --> 03:02:23,238
In fact, he spent a lot of time learning about Islam, not out of obligation,

3253
03:02:23,318 --> 03:02:25,544
but because he genuinely wants to understand.

3254
03:02:25,624 --> 03:02:28,008
He's the kind of a person who questions, reflects,

3255
03:02:28,088 --> 03:02:30,670
and needs to believe in something fully before he does.

3256
03:02:30,750 --> 03:02:34,430
before committing to it, which is one of the reasons I respect him so much.

3257
03:02:34,510 --> 03:02:38,889
He hasn't ruled out conversion, but he also wouldn't do it just to make things easier.

3258
03:02:38,969 --> 03:02:40,735
And frankly, I wouldn't want him to.

3259
03:02:40,815 --> 03:02:41,275
I'm scared,

3260
03:02:41,355 --> 03:02:47,384
scared of hurting my parents of losing them of them feeling like I've walked away from everything they raised me with.

3261
03:02:47,464 --> 03:02:50,857
I don't want to leave my faith and I don't want to leave him.

3262
03:02:50,937 --> 03:02:55,874
It feels like I'm stuck between the two halves of who I am and choosing one means losing the other.

3263
03:02:55,954 --> 03:02:57,110
My parents are starting to

3264
03:02:57,190 --> 03:03:01,399
to ask about my post-graduation plans, they'd like me to move back, settle down,

3265
03:03:01,479 --> 03:03:04,759
and get married, which in their eyes is the next logical step,

3266
03:03:04,839 --> 03:03:07,059
and I understand where they're coming from,

3267
03:03:07,139 --> 03:03:10,522
but the life I've built here is one I've worked really hard for.

3268
03:03:10,602 --> 03:03:14,244
Going back would feel like turning away from everything I've learned,

3269
03:03:14,324 --> 03:03:16,802
not just professionally, but personally as well.

3270
03:03:16,882 --> 03:03:21,142
I wish I could make everyone understand that this isn't just some European phase,

3271
03:03:21,222 --> 03:03:23,780
it's real, grounded and built on mutual respect.

3272
03:03:24,300 --> 03:03:24,806
and love.

3273
03:03:24,886 --> 03:03:31,740
I want to find a way forward that doesn't involve cutting ties or choosing between my heart and my home.

3274
03:03:31,820 --> 03:03:35,744
I know this is a lot and I've been holding off on writing this for a long time,

3275
03:03:35,824 --> 03:03:38,968
but I feel stuck between two words, between my heart, my heritage,

3276
03:03:39,048 --> 03:03:40,700
between my heart and my heritage.

3277
03:03:40,820 --> 03:03:45,900
I've reached a point where I just need to talk to someone who might understand or at least help me make sense of it all.

3278
03:03:45,980 --> 03:03:51,490
I know this email is long and a bit emotionally messy, but writing this, writing it was like taking a breath.

3279
03:03:51,570 --> 03:03:53,254
I've been holding for too long.

3280
03:03:53,334 --> 03:03:55,326
If you made it this far, thank you.

3281
03:03:55,406 --> 03:03:58,981
I truly appreciate your time and any guidance you can offer.

3282
03:03:59,061 --> 03:04:03,011
Wishing you peace, happiness and success in this world and the next.

3283
03:04:03,091 --> 03:04:03,751
Kind regards.

3284
03:04:03,831 --> 03:04:14,213
Thank you so much for your message and you write really really well which I believe you're a reader because you made it very dramatic which was fun to read nonetheless.

3285
03:04:14,293 --> 03:04:16,820
So as you heard she is a 25 year old woman.

3286
03:04:17,090 --> 03:04:23,730
She went to Europe for studies and with a degree, she found a groom which is great.

3287
03:04:23,810 --> 03:04:28,991
And the problem is that they have been in a relationship for two years,

3288
03:04:29,071 --> 03:04:33,969
the family doesn't know about it, and the family are signaling that they should come back,

3289
03:04:34,049 --> 03:04:37,850
what are the post-graduation plans, let's get you settled down, etc.

3290
03:04:37,930 --> 03:04:43,193
And the boyfriend is considering conversion, of course, not out of compulsion,

3291
03:04:43,273 --> 03:04:44,880
but out of learning about it.

3292
03:04:44,960 --> 03:04:46,880
which is the right way to do things.

3293
03:04:46,960 --> 03:04:50,880
Forcing or being forced to convert is not a good thing.

3294
03:04:50,960 --> 03:04:54,880
It's something that should be understood, read and done from the heart.

3295
03:04:54,960 --> 03:04:57,880
And it doesn't happen. But that is still under consideration.

3296
03:04:57,960 --> 03:05:01,880
In many cases, it happens that even if conversion happens,

3297
03:05:01,960 --> 03:05:07,880
because they don't happen culturally, some parents pick it difficult.

3298
03:05:07,960 --> 03:05:10,740
That everything is there, but aunt's son is not there.

3299
03:05:10,820 --> 03:05:12,740
You get what I'm saying?

3300
03:05:12,820 --> 03:05:16,740
So, now she doesn't want to walk away from the life she's built.

3301
03:05:16,820 --> 03:05:18,740
And I understand.

3302
03:05:18,820 --> 03:05:20,740
There are so many people like this, right?

3303
03:05:20,820 --> 03:05:22,740
Who have taken many dreams.

3304
03:05:22,820 --> 03:05:24,740
Europe, America, Australia.

3305
03:05:24,820 --> 03:05:26,740
Studied. They found someone.

3306
03:05:26,820 --> 03:05:28,740
They wanted to settle.

3307
03:05:28,820 --> 03:05:30,740
And then, family pressure put them back.

3308
03:05:30,820 --> 03:05:34,740
Whatever you did, you didn't just wrap it up like a carpet.

3309
03:05:34,820 --> 03:05:38,200
You wrapped it up like a yoga mat and went back to the gym.

3310
03:05:38,280 --> 03:05:44,600
and again you go back to the country and back to the land of load shedding and noise pollution.

3311
03:05:44,680 --> 03:05:51,400
How will they live? And like people who have settled down here and are living a double life in their hearts.

3312
03:05:51,480 --> 03:05:53,015
That I had all of that.

3313
03:05:53,095 --> 03:05:59,000
Things would have been this way or that way and this is where I am.

3314
03:05:59,080 --> 03:06:06,040
Anyways, could have, would have, should have, then a person keeps thinking about a thousand things. So that's not also a logical way to live.

3315
03:06:06,120 --> 03:06:09,240
and face the reality. If you don't understand, walk out.

3316
03:06:09,320 --> 03:06:14,840
Anyways, so she is stuck in a conundrum right now.

3317
03:06:14,920 --> 03:06:18,298
She hasn't told her parents yet.

3318
03:06:18,378 --> 03:06:27,340
She has told an aunt, but there, maybe she's thinking that it's just a phase.

3319
03:06:27,420 --> 03:06:33,380
Okay, do it, son. Enjoy your time. Then come back. Marriage is not with Rashid.

3320
03:06:33,460 --> 03:06:42,100
I really want to thank you all because these are extremely personal things that you are so comfortable sharing it with me.

3321
03:06:42,180 --> 03:06:44,500
This also means a lot.

3322
03:06:44,580 --> 03:06:46,701
Like he said himself,

3323
03:06:46,781 --> 03:06:52,740
it's like my breath that I have been holding for a long time has now been released.

3324
03:06:52,820 --> 03:06:55,460
That's why I always encourage you. I understand.

3325
03:06:55,540 --> 03:07:00,020
A lot of emails, a lot of people do it a lot of times, but they still get over sighted.

3326
03:07:00,100 --> 03:07:01,260
There's only so many.

3327
03:07:01,340 --> 03:07:05,100
So many emails I can read, process and give an answer to.

3328
03:07:05,180 --> 03:07:07,580
But at least writing helps.

3329
03:07:07,780 --> 03:07:13,656
So if you type out your feelings in hopes that I might come across them,

3330
03:07:13,736 --> 03:07:15,980
that's also a good feeling.

3331
03:07:16,060 --> 03:07:17,980
So please, I encourage you to write.

3332
03:07:18,060 --> 03:07:20,380
Whether I answer or not, forget about it.

3333
03:07:20,460 --> 03:07:21,580
It will happen if it is in my fate.

3334
03:07:21,660 --> 03:07:23,580
But at least don't stop yourself from writing it.

3335
03:07:23,660 --> 03:07:25,580
That's half a battle won.

3336
03:07:25,660 --> 03:07:33,420
So for your trust and honesty, I feel very validated.

3337
03:07:33,500 --> 03:07:38,620
Second thing is that you're not being reckless here.

3338
03:07:38,700 --> 03:07:43,420
You have honesty, emotional intelligence.

3339
03:07:43,500 --> 03:07:45,100
You're being respectful.

3340
03:07:45,180 --> 03:07:47,580
You're not cutting off his hands or his veins.

3341
03:07:47,660 --> 03:07:50,220
You're not saying, I'm going to read the Kalima.

3342
03:07:50,300 --> 03:07:51,580
And you're allowing him.

3343
03:07:52,020 --> 03:07:55,239
the time to reflect and consider.

3344
03:07:55,319 --> 03:08:04,740
Your dilemma is very much valid because dual citizens have a very different life.

3345
03:08:04,820 --> 03:08:10,041
They are born in a certain set of rules and conditioning,

3346
03:08:10,121 --> 03:08:16,820
they grow up and then they are exposed to a completely different environment.

3347
03:08:19,380 --> 03:08:23,060
Some things seem off-putting, some things seem better.

3348
03:08:23,140 --> 03:08:26,060
And then they come to a crossroad.

3349
03:08:26,140 --> 03:08:29,060
That meme, that I go here or there.

3350
03:08:29,140 --> 03:08:32,820
So that is a big dilemma.

3351
03:08:32,900 --> 03:08:36,500
I agree, what is called a dilemma is that, what do I choose?

3352
03:08:36,580 --> 03:08:41,060
Like, you know, my parents, they might be disappointed.

3353
03:08:41,140 --> 03:08:43,300
Okay, all these fears, I understand.

3354
03:08:43,380 --> 03:08:46,380
You know your parents better than I do. I don't know them.

3355
03:08:46,620 --> 03:08:50,460
So you know what their threshold is for disappointment.

3356
03:08:50,540 --> 03:08:53,940
Which is why you are scared and you haven't told them in two years.

3357
03:08:54,020 --> 03:08:56,100
But you never know.

3358
03:08:56,180 --> 03:09:01,780
Maybe with time, the time you are out, there has been improvement in them.

3359
03:09:01,860 --> 03:09:06,980
In the sense that tolerance and acceptability have reached some extent.

3360
03:09:07,060 --> 03:09:12,820
And we suffer more in our imagination than in real.

3361
03:09:14,150 --> 03:09:17,720
Even in my case, there were a few, you know,

3362
03:09:17,800 --> 03:09:23,870
some areas where I thought my parents would be like a big no.

3363
03:09:23,950 --> 03:09:25,621
But they were very chill.

3364
03:09:25,701 --> 03:09:26,824
So for six months,

3365
03:09:26,904 --> 03:09:34,269
my wife-to-be then fought with me that your mother is not going to accept me because of this,

3366
03:09:34,349 --> 03:09:34,870
whatever.

3367
03:09:34,950 --> 03:09:39,950
And I'm like, I haven't told them yet. So why are you fighting with me?

3368
03:09:40,560 --> 03:09:44,000
over something that doesn't exist in real, its just hypothesis.

3369
03:09:44,080 --> 03:09:49,480
Right? And then like one fine evening, I had some courage.

3370
03:09:49,560 --> 03:09:55,720
I remember in Ajman, in the car park, I kept the tea on the car's trunk and called my mother.

3371
03:09:55,800 --> 03:09:59,320
That this is the situation. She was like, okay, that's great.

3372
03:09:59,400 --> 03:10:02,440
When you get married, tell me about the sweets.

3373
03:10:02,520 --> 03:10:07,270
She was so chill. And I was like, I've been fighting for this for 8 months.

3374
03:10:08,970 --> 03:10:11,970
So in a lot of cases, we think that…

3375
03:10:13,820 --> 03:10:19,220
that maybe our parents couldn't mentally grow because after a point the mind gets stagnant

3376
03:10:19,840 --> 03:10:24,140
that this is the custom and we have to live in it, this is our tradition

3377
03:10:24,680 --> 03:10:31,680
and everything, we won't go beyond this but in a lot of cases a lot of people end up accepting a lot of things

3378
03:10:32,720 --> 03:10:34,720
for them it was like, he is getting married

3379
03:10:35,320 --> 03:10:37,320
maybe they thought, at least he is not gay

3380
03:10:38,660 --> 03:10:40,000
so okay then

3381
03:10:40,690 --> 03:10:47,256
So people with like, people who are immigrants or you know diaspora background,

3382
03:10:47,336 --> 03:10:50,010
their struggle is dual identity.

3383
03:10:50,090 --> 03:10:56,250
Like you know this is who I was for the first 22 years of my life and for the last 3 years this is who I am.

3384
03:10:56,330 --> 03:11:01,130
And I could see a projection of this life from here to here.

3385
03:11:01,210 --> 03:11:07,530
So that is a dilemma. You know your faith is there but also your relationship is there.

3386
03:11:07,780 --> 03:11:09,900
between two very important things.

3387
03:11:09,980 --> 03:11:13,660
Obviously, in a relationship, you can't be so crazy that you leave faith.

3388
03:11:13,740 --> 03:11:14,660
Okay?

3389
03:11:14,740 --> 03:11:19,294
And in faith, obviously, you have to keep a room that, you know,

3390
03:11:19,374 --> 03:11:26,685
if you can hold on to a relationship and if if both parties come to a certain common ground,

3391
03:11:26,765 --> 03:11:31,540
where your faith is not questioned or a win-win situation.

3392
03:11:31,620 --> 03:11:32,780
So I understand.

3393
03:11:32,980 --> 03:11:35,397
The rest of what you wrote,

3394
03:11:35,477 --> 03:11:43,700
it's very powerful that he is considering and he's taking time to explore.

3395
03:11:43,780 --> 03:11:49,700
Rather than out of compulsion or out of giving up for love.

3396
03:11:49,780 --> 03:11:53,700
He has to speak Arabic, four words, then the rest will be seen.

3397
03:11:53,780 --> 03:11:57,780
So it's not like that, he's actually taking time to read it.

3398
03:11:59,350 --> 03:12:01,470
converts, who are called reverts.

3399
03:12:01,550 --> 03:12:04,070
For me, they have more in their hearts.

3400
03:12:04,150 --> 03:12:06,070
We got it in inheritance.

3401
03:12:06,150 --> 03:12:08,870
The cleric gave the call to prayer in this world.

3402
03:12:08,950 --> 03:12:09,870
So we got it.

3403
03:12:09,950 --> 03:12:11,870
So we don't value it like that.

3404
03:12:11,950 --> 03:12:16,670
But after reading books, after researching for many years,

3405
03:12:16,750 --> 03:12:18,270
after going to the mosque,

3406
03:12:18,350 --> 03:12:21,270
asking questions from the Imam, how many have we seen like this?

3407
03:12:21,350 --> 03:12:25,350
Okay, let me recommend you guys something really fun.

3408
03:12:25,710 --> 03:12:34,750
There was a reality show on channel 4 called Make Me a Muslim.

3409
03:12:34,830 --> 03:12:40,750
It was like at the peak of Islamophobia.

3410
03:12:40,830 --> 03:12:44,990
It was a show. It was like a four part series or a six part series.

3411
03:12:45,070 --> 03:12:47,550
It's not available on YouTube. Make Me a Muslim.

3412
03:12:47,630 --> 03:12:53,150
So there was an Imam of Pakistani heritage in a small town in England.

3413
03:12:53,520 --> 03:13:00,000
And there was a reality show in which there was a pub owner who drank beer all day.

3414
03:13:00,080 --> 03:13:02,000
There was a stripper.

3415
03:13:02,080 --> 03:13:08,000
There was a Muslim girl whose boyfriend was a black non-Muslim.

3416
03:13:08,080 --> 03:13:13,360
And a taxi driver who was racist, sorry, he was not a bartender.

3417
03:13:13,440 --> 03:13:17,760
A taxi driver who was extremely racist, who was an alcoholic as well.

3418
03:13:17,840 --> 03:13:21,190
So all of this for six weeks.

3419
03:13:21,600 --> 03:13:22,600
Islam

3420
03:13:22,840 --> 03:13:25,820
I had to practice it. It was a very powerful show.

3421
03:13:25,900 --> 03:13:28,840
Do watch it. So in it, yes, there is also a gay in it.

3422
03:13:28,920 --> 03:13:31,800
So the gay goes home and says, brother, all this alcohol,

3423
03:13:31,880 --> 03:13:34,920
Imam Sahib puts it all in the sink.

3424
03:13:35,000 --> 03:13:37,140
He says, brother, I don't want to drink for six weeks.

3425
03:13:37,460 --> 03:13:42,520
So the stripper in it and all these people are there, then they teach them to pray.

3426
03:13:42,600 --> 03:13:45,520
Then like, they take them to the mosque, they teach them.

3427
03:13:45,600 --> 03:13:49,090
Okay, the taxi driver, because he is very racist, so he is very from the future.

3428
03:13:49,170 --> 03:13:49,470
The gay is very accepting.

3429
03:13:49,550 --> 03:13:51,971
and also there was a black girlfriend, I think it was different, this was a woman,

3430
03:13:52,051 --> 03:13:54,529
He is a full party boy.

3431
03:13:54,609 --> 03:14:03,037
So for 6 weeks or 4 weeks they gave up on alcohol, they gave up on partying.

3432
03:14:03,117 --> 03:14:04,970
They fasted.

3433
03:14:06,711 --> 03:14:16,890
a white woman who was in love with a black man.

3434
03:14:16,970 --> 03:14:19,090
in love with a Pakistani man who was a Muslim.

3435
03:14:19,170 --> 03:14:23,090
So she wants to change for him and she wants to observe it.

3436
03:14:23,170 --> 03:14:25,090
It was a very nice show.

3437
03:14:25,170 --> 03:14:27,090
It came in the late 2000s.

3438
03:14:27,170 --> 03:14:29,090
Make me a Muslim. Do watch it.

3439
03:14:29,170 --> 03:14:31,090
So way ahead of its time.

3440
03:14:31,170 --> 03:14:33,090
So it was a good show.

3441
03:14:33,170 --> 03:14:35,090
So in that it was a very good image of Islam.

3442
03:14:35,170 --> 03:14:37,090
Portrayed. Oh the Imam was very good.

3443
03:14:37,170 --> 03:14:39,170
Very acceptable and.

3444
03:14:43,250 --> 03:14:50,570
By the way, educated Imams, who we often see in reels, their approach is very different.

